    "summary": "St. Stephen > NFA > Good Lovin' monster jam",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a powerhouse second set with a seamless St. Stephen → Not Fade Away → Good Lovin' sequence and a ferocious The Other One. Jerry’s solos are unleashed, Pigpen’s organ shines forward, and the band locks into tight, high‑energy jams throughout.",
    "review": "September 18, 1970 at the Fillmore East captures the Dead in a rare burst of pure fire. After an unassuming first set that includes a surprisingly acoustic take on “Truckin’,” the second half erupts with a monumental St. Stephen → Not Fade Away → Good Lovin' suite, highlighted by Jerry’s soaring leads and Bob’s melodic guitar bursts. The Other One rolls out as a monster jam, while Pigpen’s organ sits unusually forward in the mix, giving the band an extra punch that few 1970 recordings possess. Even with occasional vocal low‑mixes and some muddy audience bleed on early tracks, the matrix‑sourced soundboard portions deliver crisp bass from Phil and a solid, driving beat from Bill Kreutzmann. The Dancin' In The Street jam adds another high‑energy peak, making this Fillmore performance one of the standout shows of the era.",
